It was mutually agreed that each member must independently develop and take ownership of their assigned component. The Team Leader would coordinate integration rather than independently developing all three modules.

5. Decisions Made

After discussion, the team collectively agreed to:

Divide the simulator into three independent processes: UI, Core and Logging.

Investigate and select an appropriate POSIX IPC mechanism.

Define communication interfaces between the processes.

Implement multithreading wherever required.

Maintain existing simulator functionality while introducing process separation.

Conduct IPC test cases to verify reliable communication.

Compare standalone and multi-process implementations through benchmarking.

Update the GitHub repository with the new architecture, implementation and documentation.

